== Step 1: convergence in B (partition :map), and the partition ==

Hypotheses (written before running). B ∈ {5, 10, 20, 40, 80, 160, 320} (B ≤ L), 40 runs per input
and B, D + Dctl (21 inputs).
 H1a. V_G before the move rises with B toward its limit (coarse blocks remove recombination inside
      blocks, so more negative LD persists between linked loci under stabilising selection and
      V_G is lower) and changes by < 3% (median |log ratio|) from 40 → 80.
 H1b. V_G at +100 changes by < 5% from B to 2B for B ≥ 40, and the survival calls (P > 1/2) differ
      in at most 1 of 21 inputs from 40 → 80 (mean |ΔP| comparable to sampling noise, ≈ 0.08).
 H1c. Because the :map partition gives every block the same share of switches, the B needed does
      not grow with L (same convergence by locus count); :position needs a larger B at the same
      accuracy (its first blocks carry most of the switches).
Convergence rule for choosing B (stated now): the smallest B in the doubling sequence such that,
from B to 2B, the median |log ratio| of V_G is < 0.03 before the move and < 0.05 at +100 and +200,
mean |ΔP| ≤ 0.10, and at most 1 of 21 threshold calls differ. Chosen by this rule alone, not by
the kernel.

