Reading. Confirmed for the variance: the block-genic variance falls under the move in both, by
the same amount (median log ratio model/kernel −0.006, −0.029, −0.026 at +50, +100, +200; per input
mostly within ±10%, worst 12000 at +200 (0.137 vs 0.249) and 14771 (dies)); and in the kernel the
block-level fall tracks the per-locus genic fall closely (e.g. 00854: 0.654 vs 0.698 at +100), so
at B = 160 the block-genic variance is a usable proxy of the genic decline that :spectrum misses.
The association statistic Σ_b Cov(G − y_b, d_b²)/bg² is small and noisy at block level with 4
kernel runs (−0.03…+0.01): mostly negative under the move in both, with a median difference of
0.000; "where measurable" it agrees, but it is not a sharp test at this resolution.

